{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfvb2B8WskWLS6JYexEGE","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Don't remove it yet. The 4% figure can't support that decision, so treat the call as \"investigate\", not \"kill\".**\n\n**Why the number is weak**\n- Five of 14 days of usage events are missing, so 4% is probably an undercount. It could be biased too, if the outage hit one platform or time window.\n- \"Tried\" isn't \"adopted\". Two weeks after a 10% rollout, 4% trying a scheduling feature could be fine or poor. Without a baseline or target, \"low\" is only a feeling.\n- Trial rate says nothing about whether the people who tried it got value or came back.\n\n**Bounded next steps (about a week)**\n1. **Recover the missing data.** Auto-scheduling creates calendar events, so backfill from server logs or the database for the five dark days. Then recompute the trial rate.\n2. **Set the bar before looking.** Compare against similar past features at the same stage, or agree on a threshold. Settle what counts as success and when you'll decide.\n3. **Look beyond trial.** Check how many users saw the entry point, how many tried it, how many completed it, how many kept the result, and how many used it again. Low reach points to a discoverability problem. Low repeat use points to a value problem.\n4. **Get qualitative signal.** Review support tickets and feedback, and talk to a few users who tried it and a few who didn't.\n\n**Decide after that**\n- Healthy repeat use among triers: improve discoverability and expand the rollout.\n- Weak even after the data is fixed: iterate or remove, with evidence behind the decision.\n\nWaiting costs little. The feature is at 10% exposure, while removing it prematurely throws away a feature that may be working."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3459,"cache_read_input_tokens":4979,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3459},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bc5b4a53-8a52-4eef-81e1-8da0dc7ad6d6","uuid":"81266d1b-2c49-4903-b3ed-2a0969cbc985","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:13:10.919Z","request_id":"req_011Cfvb2AtsNKbNEp9vgxtHN"}
